[32m+[m[32m## 1. Executive Summary & Purpose[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe **AI-Based Symptom Checker** is designed and operated strictly as an **informational health-triage aid and clinical decision-support tool**, never as a diagnostic or prescribing authority.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis document defines the binding privacy, regulatory, safety, and client-storage policies in our project. It establishes compliance with:[m
[32m+[m[32m- India's **Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act 2023)**.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Medical safety and non-diagnostic triage boundaries (**DR-01, DR-05, DR-06, DR-08**).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Progressive Web App (PWA) zero-persistence client caching rules.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEvery team member, service, frontend component, and database query must adhere to the rules defined herein.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Comprehensive Data Inventory & Classification (DR-06)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe system enforces strict data minimization. We collect and process only the minimum information necessary to execute the conversational triage flow.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2.1 Data Inventory Matrix[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Data Category | Specific Elements | Ingest Method | Processing Mode | Storage Destination | Retention Policy | Sensitivity (DPDP Act) |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Free-Text Messages** | Natural language user descriptions of symptoms | Chat input via `POST /assessments/{id}/messages` | Ephemeral; PII scrubber removes names, phones, emails, and IDs before AI extraction | PostgreSQL `messages` table (text only) | 24 hours (Guest) / Deleted on request (Account) | Sensitive Personal Data |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Extracted Symptoms** | Canonical symptom name, severity, duration, body site | Extracted by AI gateway, confirmed by user | Deterministic normalization and state tracking | PostgreSQL `symptoms` table | 24 hours (Guest) / Deleted on request (Account) | Sensitive Personal Data |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Assessment Metadata** | `id` (UUID), `state`, `created_at`, `consent_id`, `user_id` | Server generated | State machine orchestration (`START` → `COMPLETED`) | PostgreSQL `assessments` table | 24 hours (Guest) / Deleted on request (Account) | Internal / Operational |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Consent Artifacts** | `consent_id` (UUID), `policy_version`, `created_at` | `POST /consents` | Checked prior to assessment persistence | PostgreSQL `consents` table | Retained for auditability | Compliance Record |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Optional Account** | `email` (normalized), `password_hash` (Argon2) | Registration via `POST /auth/register` | Identity and authentication | PostgreSQL `users` table | Retained until account deletion | Personal Identifiable Data |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Optional Symptom Images** | Visible skin/rash photos (JPEG, PNG, WebP ≤ 5 MB) | `POST /assessments/{id}/images` | **In-memory only** (Pillow + NumPy → ONNX inference); EXIF stripped | **NEVER STORED** (zero disk, zero DB, zero logs, zero cloud bucket) | Discarded immediately after in-memory inference | High (Ephemeral Biometric / Health) |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2.2 Prohibited Data Categories (Strictly Excluded)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe following data types are **strictly out of scope** and must never be requested, ingested, or stored by any part of the application:[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Government Identifiers:** Aadhaar numbers, PAN cards, passport numbers, driver's license details.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Payment & Financial Details:** Bank accounts, UPI IDs, credit/debit cards (the tool is 100% free; no billing components).[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Doctor / Healthcare Provider Data:** Provider directories, doctor credentials, doctor schedules, booking calendars.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Third-Party Health Records:** EHR/EMR files, lab report PDFs, prescription documents.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Persistent Raw Biometric / Image Files:** No image files are ever written to disk, object storage (S3/GCS), or database blobs.[m
[32m+[m
